# crasher: the crash-test driver's protocol (drivers/test/crasher), served
# on its DR_SERVE channel, for the supervision tests (user/tests/utest/
# supervise.c): a driver that dies on command. devmgr starts it on request
# (devmgrctl.test_driver) as a supervised driver of a software device
# (devmgr's KIND_TEST); utest crashes it and checks that devmgr restarts it
# with the right backoff, that clients reconnect, and that devmgr gives up
# after too many deaths. It returns 0 when its client closes the channel.
#
# Reconnect: the driver keeps nothing across a restart. ERR_PEER_CLOSED: it
# died (it was told to, or it was killed); ask devmgr for the channel again
# (devmgr.get_service of KIND_TEST), which hands out the one the restart
# will serve.
# Format: see tools/genidl.py.

protocol crasher 92

# When this instance of the driver started (the driver's clock, uptime in
# ns), so a client sees a restart and how long it took.
1  ping   () -> (u64 started_ns)
# The driver faults (a write to the null page); the kernel kills it, like any
# crashing driver. No answer.
2  crash  () event
# The driver exits with `code`. No answer.
3  exit   (u32 code) event
